        "original_id": "3389e12a-9c4b-5a7c-81c2-779da2d10718",
        "text": "This chunk is about:\n- People: Rosario Castellanos, Arthur Hailey\n- Places: Centro Cultural Bella Época, Rosario Castellanos bookshop\n- Roles: poet, author, novelist\n- Topics: literature, bookshops\n\nFacts:\n- Arthur Hailey was born on April 5, 1920, and he was a British-Canadian novelist known for plot-driven storylines set against the backdrops of various industries.\n- Rosario Castellanos Figueroa was born on May 25, 1925, and she was a Mexican poet and author.\n- Centro Cultural Bella Época includes the Rosario Castellanos bookshop.\n- The Rosario Castellanos bookshop is claimed to be the largest bookshop in Latin America.\n- The Rosario Castellanos bookshop carries over 35 thousand different titles and has a children’s area, a coffee shop, and reading facilities.\n- Rosario Castellanos Figueroa died on August 7, 1974.\n- Arthur Hailey died on November 24, 2004.",
